WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:08.906
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:50.531
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:50.739 --> 00:52.366
[theme music concludes]

5
00:57.079 --> 00:58.831
[tender music playing]

6
01:06.088 --> 01:07.339
[breathes shakily]

7
01:07.464 --> 01:08.424
We can't.

8
01:11.010 --> 01:13.429
I can't feel any more guilty towards Namgung.

9
01:19.560 --> 01:20.519
And?

10
01:24.982 --> 01:26.775
Are you okay feeling guilty towards me?

11
01:28.527 --> 01:29.737
You said you liked it before.

12
01:31.864 --> 01:34.366
You said making people feel guilty is how you win their love.

13
01:48.464 --> 01:49.423
Get out.

14
01:50.633 --> 01:51.592
We're done here.

15
01:53.886 --> 01:55.679
[sniffles]

16
03:00.077 --> 03:01.328
[tender music concludes]

17
03:04.498 --> 03:05.457
Go on.

18
03:05.582 --> 03:06.542
It's late.

19
03:09.670 --> 03:11.255
And don't ever do this again.

20
03:15.718 --> 03:16.593
Did you clean it?

21
03:17.636 --> 03:18.846
You have to, three times a day.

22
03:19.430 --> 03:20.264
Otherwise, you'll scar.

23
03:20.389 --> 03:22.266
Doing this won't change things, Su-a.

24
03:23.100 --> 03:24.643
It only puts Manager Eom at risk.

25
03:25.644 --> 03:27.062
So stay out of this.

26
03:29.023 --> 03:30.315
Do you really want that?

27
03:32.651 --> 03:34.236
Do you really want me to stop?

28
03:35.779 --> 03:36.739
You don't.

29
03:37.031 --> 03:37.990
More than anyone else.

30
03:39.241 --> 03:41.160
You want me to fight to the end, right?

31
03:42.369 --> 03:43.370
To do what you can't.

32
03:44.121 --> 03:45.080
I know that I'm right.

33
03:45.205 --> 03:46.081
Tell me the truth.

34
03:48.292 --> 03:49.209
You're wrong.

35
03:50.961 --> 03:52.880
I'm sick of ending things this way.

36
04:05.851 --> 04:07.102
-[phone crunches] -[Su-a gasps]

37
04:13.692 --> 04:15.944
[breathes deeply]

38
04:16.695 --> 04:17.613
[sighs]

39
04:21.909 --> 04:22.826
[door opens]

40
04:23.786 --> 04:25.037
-[sighs] -[door closes]

41
04:26.163 --> 04:27.122
[Su-yeon] Where were you?

42
04:28.248 --> 04:29.208
Hmm?

43
04:31.126 --> 04:32.419
You're done?

44
04:32.544 --> 04:33.545
Are you done with rehab?

45
04:34.046 --> 04:35.756
Mmm… Mm-hmm.

46
04:36.548 --> 04:37.549
It's healed.

47
04:38.509 --> 04:39.426
[exhales deeply]

48
04:40.719 --> 04:43.263
You can stay here until you find a house.

49
04:46.433 --> 04:47.392
Are things

50
04:48.936 --> 04:49.853
fine at work?

51
04:52.856 --> 04:54.566
You've been staying late a lot.

52
04:56.110 --> 04:57.069
Take care of yourself.

53
05:04.701 --> 05:06.370
[footsteps approaching]

54
05:06.495 --> 05:07.371
[door opens]

55
05:09.915 --> 05:10.874
Why aren't you answering?

56
05:11.416 --> 05:12.376
Are you crazy?

57
05:12.751 --> 05:13.710
You shouldn't be here.

58
05:14.086 --> 05:15.254
Why did you leave, huh?

59
05:15.754 --> 05:18.048
Since when do you do what I tell you to do anyway?

60
05:19.299 --> 05:20.592
[exhales deeply]

61
05:23.971 --> 05:25.055
You know I was just mad.

62
05:26.265 --> 05:29.226
You know I've got a shitty temper, and this is what I always do.

63
05:29.643 --> 05:31.603
You know I didn't want you to actually leave!

64
05:33.063 --> 05:34.690
Why can't you give in just once?

65
05:36.316 --> 05:38.735
I gave in to you over and over again.

66
05:39.695 --> 05:41.363
Why can't you give in just once?

67
05:42.156 --> 05:43.157
[sighs]

68
05:43.407 --> 05:45.909
Hey, do you even like me at all?

69
05:48.662 --> 05:49.621
Do you give in?

70
05:50.080 --> 05:50.998
Of course I do.

71
05:51.123 --> 05:52.291
Mmm, you don't.

72
05:54.501 --> 05:56.170
I'm the one who gives in to you.

73
05:58.547 --> 06:00.215
You give in? Like hell you do.

74
06:01.800 --> 06:02.759
Look at us.

75
06:03.468 --> 06:05.304
You can come whenever, but I can't.

76
06:06.013 --> 06:08.891
Even when you're crying over Namgung, I can't even get mad.

77
06:09.683 --> 06:10.642
Tell me, Mi-do.

78
06:11.059 --> 06:12.853
Tell me when have you ever given in?

79
06:15.856 --> 06:17.566
I'm still going out with you.

80
06:18.734 --> 06:19.776
[emotional music playing]

81
06:20.527 --> 06:23.614
You asked whether I'd save Namgung or my own dad,

82
06:25.324 --> 06:26.742
and I'm still seeing you.

83
06:30.746 --> 06:35.209
You tore open my worst wound, and I'm still seeing you.

84
06:38.003 --> 06:40.505
I'm hurting someone more precious than my life.

85
06:41.715 --> 06:43.050
But I'm still seeing you.

86
06:43.884 --> 06:45.177
[music rises]

87
07:14.831 --> 07:15.707
Move.

88
07:16.208 --> 07:17.292
It's my fault.

89
07:19.628 --> 07:20.963
I said it's my fault!

90
07:25.342 --> 07:26.301
[Tae-seung] No, it's not.

91
07:28.428 --> 07:29.638
Mi-do, it's not your fault.

92
07:33.016 --> 07:34.142
I'm the one to blame.

93
07:47.572 --> 07:48.532
Hilarious.

94
07:51.702 --> 07:53.370
Mi-do really is giving in.

95
08:26.820 --> 08:28.280
[music swells]

96
08:38.623 --> 08:39.666
[music softens]

97
09:16.161 --> 09:20.040
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

98
09:20.165 --> 09:24.544
WHO DO WE LOVE THE MOST?

99
09:24.711 --> 09:26.004
[emotional music concludes]

100
09:27.172 --> 09:28.256
[Tae-seung] Are you okay?

101
09:29.424 --> 09:31.093
LEE MI-DO

102
09:35.514 --> 09:37.432
Is Namgung always that hot-headed?

103
09:41.645 --> 09:42.771
[sighs deeply]

104
09:45.148 --> 09:45.982
Hmm.

105
09:48.110 --> 09:50.112
Why are you giving in to me?

106
09:50.237 --> 09:51.863
-[knock on door] -Yeah?

107
09:52.322 --> 09:53.198
[door opens]

108
09:54.658 --> 09:56.618
[Ju-hyeok] Hi there. Wow.

109
09:57.244 --> 09:58.787
It's shabbier than I thought.

110
10:00.497 --> 10:01.456
Hmm?

111
10:13.593 --> 10:15.178
The Taegye-ri wind farm project

112
10:16.430 --> 10:17.389
Sabotage it.

113
10:19.975 --> 10:23.019
My father-in-law's district desperately needs that project.

114
10:23.812 --> 10:24.771
[exhales wearily]

115
10:27.524 --> 10:28.567
I'm aware of it.

116
10:30.318 --> 10:33.280
Goyeong became the second choice because of Taegye-ri.

117
10:35.866 --> 10:38.827
Oh… [laughs] …CEO Seo or…

118
10:40.036 --> 10:44.207
Mr. Seo Ju-hyeok, I've been keeping tabs on your dear father-in-law,

119
10:45.125 --> 10:46.918
and I have a good guess why you're here.

120
10:48.170 --> 10:49.713
[chuckles]

121
10:50.922 --> 10:52.966
I need a lawyer for the Taegye-ri project, huh?

122
10:53.508 --> 10:55.343
-No one's better suited than you. -[scoffs]

123
10:56.511 --> 10:58.805
Just talk them into registering a business

124
10:58.930 --> 11:02.309
to get the land compensation, and I'll handle the rest.

125
11:03.935 --> 11:05.687
Ah, how evil.

126
11:07.439 --> 11:08.857
Tossing people like that.

127
11:09.483 --> 11:10.442
I want to do it.

128
11:12.110 --> 11:15.947
And I'm allowed to do what I want.

129
11:18.950 --> 11:20.035
[disconcerting music playing]

130
11:25.332 --> 11:26.791
Just show your cards already.

131
11:27.876 --> 11:28.960
I know how you work.

132
11:31.922 --> 11:32.881
Director Mi-do.

133
11:35.967 --> 11:36.927
How is she?

134
11:37.969 --> 11:38.929
You love her?

135
11:45.727 --> 11:46.686
I'm disappointed.

136
11:47.437 --> 11:49.314
All you have dug up is my love life?

137
11:49.814 --> 11:52.400
You found someone I saw out of boredom, really.

138
11:52.776 --> 11:53.652
[scoffs]

139
11:53.777 --> 11:54.778
Is that all you got?

140
11:54.903 --> 11:56.488
I am also disappointed,

141
11:57.864 --> 11:58.823
Han Tae-seung,

142
12:00.200 --> 12:04.162
and you have been talking way too long.

143
12:04.538 --> 12:05.580
[music rises]

144
12:06.957 --> 12:08.833
You must do what you've been told.

145
12:16.091 --> 12:17.717
[exhales deeply]

146
12:20.887 --> 12:22.013
-[phone chimes] -[sighs]

147
12:22.556 --> 12:23.807
LEE SI-WOO, CORP. FINANCE 2

148
12:23.974 --> 12:25.058
[Attorney Lee] Yes, sir?

149
12:26.184 --> 12:29.646
Hey, Lee Mi-do's mother's place.

150
12:30.313 --> 12:33.483
Just as we discussed, please file for demolition,

151
12:33.608 --> 12:35.777
restitution, and damages. Everything.

152
12:36.403 --> 12:38.697
Attach the survey on encroachment and apply

153
12:39.406 --> 12:40.574
for provisional disposition.

154
12:41.449 --> 12:42.534
Oh, and earlier, I--

155
12:42.659 --> 12:43.743
[call drops]

156
12:48.748 --> 12:49.583
[laughs]

157
12:51.626 --> 12:52.877
[disconcerting music concludes]

158
12:53.545 --> 12:55.797
-[Jang-mi] The pacing drags too much. -[Mi-do] You said three minutes.

159
12:55.922 --> 12:57.048
It's three minutes long.

160
12:57.591 --> 13:00.051
No, I meant the first ten seconds drag on too long.

161
13:00.176 --> 13:01.386
-Huh? -Look, Director Lee,

162
13:01.511 --> 13:03.471
it's just like I said, the B-roll is too long.

163
13:03.597 --> 13:05.098
The drop-off rate will skyrocket, huh?

164
13:05.765 --> 13:06.975
Look, this isn't a movie.

165
13:07.350 --> 13:08.643
Cutting shots won't help.

166
13:09.144 --> 13:12.147
You need jump cuts here to pick up and accelerate the tempo.

167
13:13.898 --> 13:15.108
Never mind. We'll do it.

168
13:15.233 --> 13:16.526
-Yeah, we'll do it. -[sighs]

169
13:19.571 --> 13:20.864
[spirited music playing]

170
13:24.034 --> 13:24.909
[sighs]

171
13:25.035 --> 13:27.662
We didn't mean to be rude, Director Lee.

172
13:27.787 --> 13:29.414
We went too far. We're very sorry.

173
13:29.539 --> 13:31.249
And I didn't mean to sigh, Director.

174
13:31.374 --> 13:32.459
I didn't sleep well.

175
13:32.584 --> 13:33.460
I had nightmares.

176
13:33.585 --> 13:35.545
Hmm. Call it as it is.

177
13:36.379 --> 13:37.297
Hmm.

178
13:39.049 --> 13:40.008
You're being harsh?

179
13:40.842 --> 13:41.801
That's fine.

180
13:42.052 --> 13:43.428
Better than not knowing.

181
13:45.013 --> 13:47.307
Your blatant attitude bugged me a little.

182
13:48.224 --> 13:51.895
But given how I treated you, I'll let it slide as payback.

183
13:53.188 --> 13:57.359
As for the sigh, I'll consider it a bodily function.

184
13:58.652 --> 13:59.819
But…

185
14:02.530 --> 14:04.866
If you're going to teach me, do it right.

186
14:05.867 --> 14:07.952
Like I taught you guys properly.

187
14:08.078 --> 14:08.912
Hmm?

188
14:12.624 --> 14:13.750
Let's take five.

189
14:14.542 --> 14:15.877
You can badmouth me.

190
14:18.421 --> 14:21.341
[groaning]

191
14:22.133 --> 14:23.802
Why did you have to sigh?

192
14:23.927 --> 14:25.136
Why would you talk like that?

193
14:25.845 --> 14:27.305
[spirited music concludes]

194
14:28.056 --> 14:29.307
[sighs deeply]

195
14:31.476 --> 14:33.019
[phone vibrating]

196
14:36.272 --> 14:38.316
TAK JACKSON

197
14:41.444 --> 14:42.654
[phone vibrates]

198
14:44.614 --> 14:46.741
[Se-young] Hey Mi-do, you still alive?

199
14:47.117 --> 14:49.452
-[phone vibrates] -[Se-young] Are you avoiding me too?

200
14:49.577 --> 14:50.537
Ghosting me?

201
14:50.662 --> 14:52.455
-[phone vibrates] -[Se-young] You're a traitor.

202
14:52.580 --> 14:53.915
Reaching three million?

203
14:54.040 --> 14:54.958
What's the point?

204
14:55.083 --> 14:56.334
-[phone vibrates] -[Se-young] Ugh!

205
14:56.459 --> 14:57.627
Might as well make it four.

206
14:58.253 --> 14:59.379
I'm so bored.

207
14:59.504 --> 15:00.505
And lonely.

208
15:00.630 --> 15:01.715
[phone vibrates]

209
15:03.007 --> 15:04.426
[Se-young] Is this your boyfriend's company?

210
15:09.931 --> 15:11.433
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

211
15:11.641 --> 15:14.352
CHEAP IMPORTED SWEET POTATO SWAP UNCOVERED

212
15:14.519 --> 15:15.645
[tense music playing]

213
15:18.398 --> 15:19.733
Did you see this article?

214
15:20.734 --> 15:23.194
-[employee 1] What's this? Is this fake? -[employee 2 gasps]

215
15:23.653 --> 15:25.363
I think things might get out of hand.

216
15:25.947 --> 15:28.032
[employee 3] The company didn't know this?

217
15:28.283 --> 15:30.785
-[phone rings] -Hello? Hunmin Confectionery.

218
15:30.910 --> 15:32.287
Oh no, that is false.

219
15:32.412 --> 15:34.080
Can you hold for a moment? Sorry about that.

220
15:35.039 --> 15:37.751
Regarding the returns, we're currently looking into the matter.

221
15:38.293 --> 15:39.419
Rest assured that you'll have

222
15:39.544 --> 15:40.879
-an answer soon. -It's not confirmed yet?

223
15:41.004 --> 15:42.630
[employee 4] Who's the whistleblower?

224
15:42.756 --> 15:43.715
We're done.

225
15:43.840 --> 15:44.841
The stock's going to tank.

226
15:45.508 --> 15:46.342
What do we do?

227
15:46.801 --> 15:47.927
[Su-a panting]

228
15:59.564 --> 16:00.523
Are things…

229
16:02.692 --> 16:03.651
fine at work?

230
16:04.444 --> 16:06.279
[music rises]

231
16:11.242 --> 16:13.328
[voicemail] The number you have dialed is not available.

232
16:13.453 --> 16:14.996
Please leave a message after the tone.

233
16:16.998 --> 16:18.124
[Su-a] You did this, right?

234
16:18.249 --> 16:19.209
I won't forgive you.

235
16:19.918 --> 16:21.753
I will never, ever forgive you this time.

236
16:22.253 --> 16:23.296
I'm going to the police.

237
16:24.088 --> 16:25.131
I'm suing you.

238
16:25.256 --> 16:27.008
MR. NAMGUNG

239
16:27.133 --> 16:31.137
[phone vibrating]

240
16:46.986 --> 16:48.905
[phone vibrating]

241
16:49.030 --> 16:50.281
MR. NAMGUNG

242
16:54.661 --> 16:55.954
[tense music concludes]

243
16:56.538 --> 16:58.456
[Namgung] Straight up ignoring my calls, huh?

244
17:04.462 --> 17:05.421
What's up?

245
17:15.348 --> 17:17.183
Still haven't found Bambi a home.

246
17:18.142 --> 17:19.435
I can imagine why.

247
17:20.228 --> 17:22.730
You were probably super strict and rejected them all.

248
17:24.399 --> 17:26.568
The company will put out a rebuttal tomorrow.

249
17:27.026 --> 17:29.445
The usual playbook, smear the whistleblower.

250
17:30.154 --> 17:33.199
They'll say they leaked all the information just for the money,

251
17:33.324 --> 17:35.577
so the claims can't be trusted.

252
17:36.578 --> 17:37.537
Totally predictable.

253
17:37.912 --> 17:38.913
I didn't leak anything.

254
17:39.622 --> 17:40.623
I really didn't.

255
17:40.748 --> 17:42.208
I know. It wasn't you.

256
17:46.421 --> 17:47.380
Who was it?

257
17:49.007 --> 17:50.008
Who took your files?

258
17:58.725 --> 18:00.351
The company already has records

259
18:01.603 --> 18:05.565
of payment from two outlets naming Team 3's Park Su-a

260
18:06.649 --> 18:08.735
with proof confirming your ID.

261
18:08.860 --> 18:10.403
Unless something changes,

262
18:11.571 --> 18:13.364
you'll face the disciplinary panel

263
18:13.698 --> 18:17.410
to answer for trade secret ethics violations and bribery,

264
18:20.288 --> 18:21.623
then a police investigation.

265
18:24.167 --> 18:25.126
So tell me.

266
18:27.211 --> 18:28.171
You know who it is.

267
18:31.466 --> 18:32.842
[soft music playing]

268
18:36.346 --> 18:37.305
I caused this.

269
18:39.223 --> 18:40.183
I'll handle it.

270
18:40.808 --> 18:42.268
How are you going to handle it?

271
18:44.938 --> 18:46.773
Things are bad, don't you get what I'm telling you?

272
18:46.898 --> 18:47.774
I do.

273
18:48.942 --> 18:50.944
I do, so please do not get involved.

274
18:55.198 --> 18:59.410
Manager Eom told me the phone data wasn't recovered.

275
19:00.787 --> 19:02.664
You'll get in trouble if you stay involved.

276
19:05.583 --> 19:06.417
And…

277
19:08.378 --> 19:10.129
I believe I couldn't bear that.

278
19:11.631 --> 19:12.590
So please,

279
19:14.717 --> 19:15.927
stay out of it, please.

280
19:23.351 --> 19:25.144
I really thought I could get to the bottom of this.

281
19:26.729 --> 19:27.897
I really did.

282
19:29.023 --> 19:29.899
But…

283
19:30.858 --> 19:32.527
I guess I was mistaken.

284
19:35.697 --> 19:37.365
I really was mistaken.

285
19:51.379 --> 19:55.883
[phone vibrating]

286
19:58.261 --> 20:00.430
YEONG-DO

287
20:01.264 --> 20:02.849
[phone vibrating]

288
20:02.974 --> 20:04.267
[soft music concludes]

289
20:05.351 --> 20:07.770
[sirens wailing]

290
20:12.900 --> 20:14.777
[doctor] His vitals have all stabilized now.

291
20:16.029 --> 20:18.489
We need some more tests to make sure there's no complications,

292
20:18.614 --> 20:20.408
so be sure to get them done.

293
20:20.658 --> 20:21.701
[Yeong-do] Yes, thank you.

294
20:23.995 --> 20:25.204
[exhales deeply]

295
20:39.343 --> 20:41.429
Living like a corpse wasn't enough for you,

296
20:41.554 --> 20:43.389
so now you got a death wish or what is it?

297
20:44.599 --> 20:46.851
Even as a pro, I'd black out once a year.

298
20:47.310 --> 20:48.269
It's no big deal.

299
20:48.644 --> 20:51.147
Looking for Baek Bo-ra's music box or whatever,

300
20:51.272 --> 20:52.482
tell me you'll stop now.

301
20:53.149 --> 20:54.609
Or I'm telling Mom everything!

302
20:54.984 --> 20:55.943
I mean it!

303
20:56.277 --> 20:57.487
You'd want to give her a heart attack?

304
20:58.613 --> 20:59.697
You little punk!

305
20:59.822 --> 21:00.948
I just left the ER.

306
21:01.616 --> 21:02.575
Two hours ago.

307
21:04.702 --> 21:06.162
Jeez. [scoffs]

308
21:07.038 --> 21:08.539
Why aren't you saying anything?

309
21:10.666 --> 21:11.918
Oh, Mi-do.

310
21:14.712 --> 21:15.671
Where are you going?

311
21:17.173 --> 21:18.132
Hey.

312
21:18.257 --> 21:19.217
Oh, shit.

313
21:21.719 --> 21:22.762
[upbeat music playing]

314
21:22.887 --> 21:23.846
[Wan-do grunts]

315
21:23.971 --> 21:25.223
Help, help, help!

316
21:25.348 --> 21:27.517
Help me out here, bro! Ah!

317
21:28.267 --> 21:31.229
[grunting]

318
21:31.687 --> 21:33.564
-Tie him up, tie him up. -[Wan-do] I can't see. Hey, hey!

319
21:33.689 --> 21:34.941
Bro! Bro, I can't see anything!

320
21:35.066 --> 21:37.485
-[Yeong-do] Hit him, Mi-do! -[Wan-do groaning]

321
21:37.610 --> 21:38.611
Ow! [groans]

322
21:42.240 --> 21:43.574
-[microphone feedback whines] -Are you crazy?

323
21:43.699 --> 21:44.700
No! Cut it out.

324
21:45.243 --> 21:46.369
[yelps] Are you insane?

325
21:46.911 --> 21:48.621
Psycho! What are you doing?!

326
21:48.746 --> 21:52.041
Stop it! [groans, winces]

327
21:52.166 --> 21:54.043
Don't just watch! Stop her! Hold on!

328
21:54.168 --> 21:56.754
Hey, hey, Mi-do. All right, stop. That's enough for now.

329
21:59.173 --> 22:00.550
[upbeat music concludes]

330
22:00.675 --> 22:03.427
You two live however you want, so why can't I do the same?

331
22:03.553 --> 22:04.804
Why? Why?!

332
22:06.430 --> 22:07.390
Hey, Mi-do.

333
22:07.682 --> 22:08.683
Don't stop.

334
22:08.808 --> 22:09.767
Beat him up!

335
22:10.059 --> 22:11.352
This crazy dipshit is nuts!

336
22:11.769 --> 22:12.895
Go for it, Mi-do!

337
22:14.105 --> 22:15.064
Now listen.

338
22:15.398 --> 22:17.066
Say you'll never go in the water.

339
22:17.191 --> 22:18.734
[breathing shakily]

340
22:22.071 --> 22:23.030
No.

341
22:23.865 --> 22:25.199
[scoffs]

342
22:26.367 --> 22:27.326
You little idiot!

343
22:30.538 --> 22:31.706
He's your brother.

344
22:32.498 --> 22:34.125
Think this will make him listen to you?

345
22:34.250 --> 22:36.836
[breathing deeply]

346
22:46.220 --> 22:47.346
Only go on weekends.

347
22:48.014 --> 22:48.973
I'll go with you.

348
22:51.434 --> 22:53.144
I'll stop them from beating you up.

349
22:53.895 --> 22:54.854
Hey!

350
22:56.856 --> 22:57.899
Answer me.

351
23:06.240 --> 23:08.618
Yeah. [breathes shakily]

352
23:12.538 --> 23:14.123
[exhales deeply]

353
23:16.334 --> 23:17.418
[sighs]

354
23:20.504 --> 23:22.048
[door bell tinkles]

355
23:22.173 --> 23:23.216
[door closes]

356
23:31.015 --> 23:32.850
[soft, somber music playing]

357
23:34.602 --> 23:35.561
Come on, Bo-ra!

358
23:36.771 --> 23:37.980
Why are you here, huh?

359
23:38.397 --> 23:39.357
I was so worried.

360
23:39.649 --> 23:40.816
You mean so annoyed.

361
23:42.860 --> 23:43.819
What?

362
23:45.696 --> 23:46.656
Am I wrong?

363
23:49.200 --> 23:50.243
What do you mean?

364
23:50.368 --> 23:51.410
Stop accusing me.

365
23:51.535 --> 23:53.120
[Bo-ra] Don't look at me like that.

366
23:53.996 --> 23:56.666
Don't look at me like you're sick of caring for me.

367
24:01.921 --> 24:03.923
You shouldn't have saved me then.

368
24:05.132 --> 24:07.677
You should have just let me die then.

369
24:10.221 --> 24:13.724
Then I'd remember you as the Lee Wan-do who loved me.

370
24:18.312 --> 24:19.146
The music box.

371
24:21.983 --> 24:23.818
I threw it into Seokchon Lake.

372
24:27.446 --> 24:28.406
You know

373
24:30.741 --> 24:32.535
that I can't sleep without it.

374
24:37.248 --> 24:38.874
When I die, please find it.

375
24:42.378 --> 24:43.546
If you don't…

376
24:46.465 --> 24:49.093
even in death, I'll never rest because of you.

377
24:57.018 --> 24:58.519
[music swells]

378
25:02.690 --> 25:04.150
[sniffles]

379
25:06.861 --> 25:07.820
Please, Bo-ra.

380
25:12.408 --> 25:14.035
Are you still not resting…

381
25:18.414 --> 25:19.373
because of me?

382
25:24.003 --> 25:25.921
Are you still not at peace?

383
25:40.686 --> 25:42.271
[soft, somber music concludes]

384
26:00.998 --> 26:02.291
How many feet today?

385
26:04.960 --> 26:05.920
Six hundred feet.

386
26:06.587 --> 26:09.131
Or maybe 800.

387
26:12.343 --> 26:13.302
Sorry.

388
26:14.303 --> 26:15.388
I made you worry.

389
26:17.431 --> 26:18.391
But look,

390
26:19.850 --> 26:20.976
I'm struggling.

391
26:24.814 --> 26:25.856
It's very difficult.

392
26:29.318 --> 26:31.404
I tried to hold out until the fifth anniversary

393
26:31.529 --> 26:33.572
of Bo-ra's death, but I can't do this.

394
26:38.661 --> 26:40.204
Don't use Bo-ra as a pretext.

395
26:41.247 --> 26:42.081
Stop lying.

396
26:43.666 --> 26:47.378
Since you had inner ear barotrauma six years ago, your time's dropped,

397
26:47.503 --> 26:50.673
your rank of course fell, and you never got your old form back.

398
26:51.757 --> 26:54.135
Right when you had to end your athletic career,

399
26:54.552 --> 26:57.304
at your most hopeless moment, Bo-ra died.

400
27:02.184 --> 27:03.936
Your feelings for her include guilt.

401
27:04.478 --> 27:05.479
That's part of it.

402
27:05.813 --> 27:06.772
Of course it is.

403
27:06.897 --> 27:08.482
Listen to me now, Wan-do.

404
27:12.570 --> 27:14.864
If you're sorry for her, don't live like this.

405
27:15.781 --> 27:17.408
She'd be so heartbroken.

406
27:18.659 --> 27:23.289
If she saw you using her as an excuse, it would break her heart.

407
27:34.258 --> 27:35.676
[door bell tinkles]

408
27:38.220 --> 27:40.222
[gentle music playing]

409
27:45.603 --> 27:47.438
His CT and MRI came back normal.

410
27:48.230 --> 27:50.858
[breathes deeply]

411
27:52.026 --> 27:54.612
[Namgung] You know he won't stop just because we tell him to.

412
27:55.571 --> 27:58.782
I'll take responsibility for Wan-do, so he'll be fine.

413
28:01.243 --> 28:04.079
Are you really going to dive with Wan-do on weekends?

414
28:05.414 --> 28:06.832
You know I'm certified.

415
28:08.709 --> 28:10.669
I'm not afraid of water like you.

416
28:14.924 --> 28:16.592
I think you pushed through it…

417
28:19.345 --> 28:20.429
because of me.

418
28:22.223 --> 28:25.267
You were scared, and you pushed through it anyway.

419
28:28.229 --> 28:32.358
When Wan-do first said he wanted to swim and I agreed,

420
28:33.817 --> 28:35.361
you started swimming lessons.

421
28:37.780 --> 28:38.948
I know it all.

422
28:41.659 --> 28:42.618
Namgung,

423
28:43.744 --> 28:46.080
you'd do anything for me, I know.

424
28:47.665 --> 28:48.916
And I'd do it too.

425
28:51.585 --> 28:52.795
But you know what?

426
28:58.092 --> 29:00.177
At least I lived for myself.

427
29:01.387 --> 29:02.471
Even with movies.

428
29:03.430 --> 29:04.723
I did what I wanted.

429
29:05.516 --> 29:07.893
And saw it through to the very end.

430
29:09.478 --> 29:11.230
[inhales deeply]

431
29:11.355 --> 29:12.398
You never did that.

432
29:15.568 --> 29:17.486
[music swells]

433
29:22.825 --> 29:23.951
I regret it.

434
29:28.247 --> 29:30.583
I really regret telling you something.

435
29:34.086 --> 29:35.087
To not like her.

436
29:45.014 --> 29:46.098
Namgung…

437
29:49.560 --> 29:50.769
do whatever you want.

438
29:54.898 --> 29:56.609
Do what you truly desire.

439
29:57.276 --> 29:58.611
Whatever you decide, Namgung.

440
30:02.114 --> 30:03.699
Do whatever you want.

441
30:06.827 --> 30:08.495
Don't even think about me.

442
30:10.789 --> 30:11.749
Just…

443
30:13.083 --> 30:14.043
do it.

444
30:24.053 --> 30:25.262
[gentle music concludes]

445
30:25.387 --> 30:30.059
DAMUNGOL THE WORST NOODLE SHOP IN TOWN ONLY TOTAL SUCKERS EAT HERE

446
30:30.225 --> 30:31.685
Look, look, look, look.

447
30:31.810 --> 30:33.103
What are you going to do about this?

448
30:33.354 --> 30:34.271
Huh?

449
30:34.396 --> 30:36.106
I can't just let this slide.

450
30:36.774 --> 30:37.983
[Yeong-do] I apologize.

451
30:38.108 --> 30:40.277
I will send someone to clean it right away.

452
30:40.778 --> 30:41.737
I'm sorry.

453
30:41.987 --> 30:43.697
Ah, father, why are you sorry?

454
30:44.281 --> 30:45.240
He started this to…

455
30:47.576 --> 30:49.203
And mom, he insulted her.

456
30:49.703 --> 30:51.205
Calling her a greedy tutoring witch.

457
30:51.497 --> 30:52.456
Hey, Sang-su.

458
30:53.123 --> 30:54.458
[sighs wearily]

459
30:55.709 --> 30:56.669
We apologize.

460
30:56.794 --> 30:57.878
[huffs]

461
31:05.135 --> 31:06.220
[sighs]

462
31:11.892 --> 31:13.352
Just go. I will handle it.

463
31:14.770 --> 31:15.729
And how?

464
31:16.063 --> 31:17.022
With money?

465
31:19.191 --> 31:20.150
Mun-yeong…

466
31:22.611 --> 31:26.490
do you remember the 47 vows I made when I proposed to you?

467
31:26.615 --> 31:29.243
With all of your sub-clauses, there were 52.

468
31:29.368 --> 31:31.161
[chuckles softly]

469
31:31.412 --> 31:32.371
Right, 52.

470
31:34.957 --> 31:38.377
I couldn't keep them all, but I will keep this one…

471
31:41.422 --> 31:43.507
to be a good father to Sang-su.

472
31:46.885 --> 31:48.053
I will honor that.

473
31:56.061 --> 31:57.020
Mun-yeong,

474
31:58.731 --> 31:59.857
congrats on your wedding.

475
32:01.358 --> 32:02.443
I wish you joy.

476
32:05.195 --> 32:06.113
Okay.

477
32:16.790 --> 32:17.750
Hey.

478
32:18.584 --> 32:19.585
What?

479
32:19.710 --> 32:20.669
What do you want?

480
32:20.794 --> 32:21.712
To know if I'm happy?

481
32:22.296 --> 32:25.883
Uh, just check who is the beneficiary of the insurance.

482
32:26.884 --> 32:28.969
Why is a young handsome guy dating you?

483
32:29.595 --> 32:30.846
Vet him before the wedding.

484
32:31.346 --> 32:32.681
I can get a PI if you want to.

485
32:33.432 --> 32:34.600
Why you little…

486
32:35.476 --> 32:36.435
Hey!

487
32:36.935 --> 32:38.729
[jaunty music playing]

488
32:49.281 --> 32:50.365
[sighs]

489
32:56.497 --> 32:59.416
[Yeong-do] Your mom was a really good teacher.

490
33:00.042 --> 33:03.879
If not for her chronic IBS, she would have been a professor.

491
33:06.298 --> 33:08.550
And your mom donates the most among celebrity instructors,

492
33:09.134 --> 33:11.345
almost as if her son's inheritance doesn't matter.

493
33:13.722 --> 33:17.643
As long as you know whatever people say about your mom

494
33:17.768 --> 33:20.020
calling her money-crazy, greedy, or things like that,

495
33:20.145 --> 33:23.398
you just need to know she isn't like that at all.

496
33:23.816 --> 33:25.609
So we're just going to do nothing?

497
33:27.194 --> 33:30.697
Dad, I held back because I didn't want to freak you out.

498
33:33.158 --> 33:34.785
I never said I'd sit around doing nothing.

499
33:36.453 --> 33:37.412
Look, son.

500
33:38.038 --> 33:39.706
You should have called your dad for this.

501
33:41.083 --> 33:42.125
And for graffiti.

502
33:43.627 --> 33:45.045
You gotta use industrial grade.

503
33:46.380 --> 33:47.339
You feel me?

504
33:50.801 --> 33:53.011
BROTHER CLEANING

505
33:54.346 --> 33:55.264
What do I put?

506
33:55.931 --> 33:58.183
-Star instructor, Ko Mun-yeong. -Gotcha.

507
34:02.563 --> 34:03.522
[Sang-su chuckles]

508
34:03.647 --> 34:07.025
[laughs]

509
34:07.276 --> 34:08.235
[jaunty music concludes]

510
34:13.365 --> 34:16.827
So, why didn't you follow the reporting procedures?

511
34:18.787 --> 34:20.122
I couldn't trust them.

512
34:22.082 --> 34:24.960
Listen, Park Su-a, this is your subjective judgment.

513
34:25.085 --> 34:29.423
Our policy dictates that matters like this be handled through internal channels.

514
34:29.798 --> 34:31.091
According to policy,

515
34:31.925 --> 34:34.511
you should have investigated the corruption suspects first.

516
34:35.137 --> 34:40.058
Regarding that, our wonderful audit team is currently investigating the facts.

517
34:40.183 --> 34:43.562
Then, have you investigated me already?

518
34:47.733 --> 34:50.068
On the date and time the Gangmu Daily reporter

519
34:50.193 --> 34:55.574
claimed I gave him the files, did you check my attendance records?

520
34:56.283 --> 35:00.287
Did you check whether the USB files given to reporters were fabricated

521
35:01.079 --> 35:03.957
or perhaps even leaked without authorization?

522
35:05.208 --> 35:06.168
Hmm.

523
35:08.045 --> 35:10.672
To this committee with no procedural legitimacy,

524
35:10.797 --> 35:12.716
I will not explain a single thing.

525
35:14.217 --> 35:16.011
If you want my explanation,

526
35:16.887 --> 35:19.056
do a proper investigation by the rules first.

527
35:21.558 --> 35:22.601
[Ho-sik sighs]

528
35:22.726 --> 35:23.685
It's for the best.

529
35:25.437 --> 35:28.774
Once I gathered all the files, I was going to offer them up

530
35:28.899 --> 35:31.860
to an executive I trust and ride their coattails.

531
35:33.612 --> 35:35.072
But everyone is corrupt.

532
35:35.948 --> 35:36.990
Is having good character

533
35:37.115 --> 35:40.160
and being competent while being squeaky clean really hard?

534
35:41.078 --> 35:42.037
God.

535
35:43.747 --> 35:44.957
Forget about it.

536
35:45.332 --> 35:46.583
It's over anyway.

537
35:47.918 --> 35:48.877
[sighs]

538
35:49.544 --> 35:51.546
Just forget about work and be a good father.

539
35:55.467 --> 35:57.052
That alone is a huge task.

540
36:01.515 --> 36:04.601
I'm not a great dad to my poor kid.

541
36:08.939 --> 36:10.983
Lately, I lose my temper.

542
36:12.192 --> 36:13.151
What am I doing?

543
36:15.445 --> 36:17.322
I wanna quit all the time, huh?

544
36:17.614 --> 36:19.950
I think about it hundreds of times a day.

545
36:20.617 --> 36:22.786
I gotta pay for the piano lessons.

546
36:22.911 --> 36:23.912
[sighs]

547
36:24.496 --> 36:26.331
[sentimental guitar music playing]

548
36:27.541 --> 36:30.585
Suddenly, I had a strange thought.

549
36:31.753 --> 36:32.963
Who told me to live like this?

550
36:33.755 --> 36:34.715
Huh?

551
36:37.843 --> 36:40.595
At this rate, I might end up…

552
36:42.931 --> 36:43.890
hating Su-min.

553
36:45.017 --> 36:46.309
Because of that, I wanted…

554
36:48.979 --> 36:50.230
to live on my terms.

555
36:50.731 --> 36:52.649
I really wanted to go all in on life,

556
36:53.066 --> 36:55.736
so I took the plunge and did what I knew was right.

557
36:57.320 --> 36:58.405
Damn it.

558
36:59.072 --> 37:00.115
[chuckles]

559
37:00.949 --> 37:01.950
And I don't regret it.

560
37:02.617 --> 37:03.827
I'm happy.

561
37:05.203 --> 37:06.413
I feel so relieved.

562
37:10.292 --> 37:11.460
[exhales deeply]

563
37:14.463 --> 37:16.757
Really, such a relief.

564
37:24.806 --> 37:27.809
Fine! I do regret it, you bastard, huh?

565
37:28.310 --> 37:29.561
Why didn't you stop me?

566
37:29.686 --> 37:30.896
You know how I get.

567
37:31.021 --> 37:32.064
Why didn't you stop me?

568
37:32.689 --> 37:34.357
You have my wife's number.

569
37:34.483 --> 37:36.109
You could have called her, you idiot.

570
37:36.526 --> 37:37.861
Why didn't you call her?

571
37:39.071 --> 37:40.030
Why?

572
37:40.155 --> 37:41.114
Why didn't you stop…

573
37:41.239 --> 37:42.074
Why?

574
37:44.910 --> 37:46.119
I was rooting for you.

575
37:49.998 --> 37:50.957
I truly was.

576
37:53.126 --> 37:55.629
Because I wanted you to make director.

577
38:09.810 --> 38:10.977
[sobs softly]

578
38:15.398 --> 38:16.942
[sentimental guitar music concludes]

579
38:17.067 --> 38:19.194
That will double the current payout.

580
38:19.694 --> 38:20.570
Double it.

581
38:20.695 --> 38:21.947
Double? Oh!

582
38:22.072 --> 38:25.951
So you mean that to get more than the land compensation,

583
38:26.076 --> 38:28.995
we'll need to register a business, is that it?

584
38:29.121 --> 38:30.080
Exactly.

585
38:30.580 --> 38:31.623
Sell it as forest land,

586
38:31.748 --> 38:33.416
it's 20,000 won per square foot.

587
38:33.542 --> 38:35.293
That will seem like pocket change.

588
38:36.253 --> 38:37.838
But as a business site, you'll make more.

589
38:38.880 --> 38:41.508
You will all be able to earn millions.

590
38:41.758 --> 38:42.717
Millions?

591
38:42.843 --> 38:46.513
On top of the land payout, you'll get an extra juicy compensation

592
38:47.097 --> 38:48.640
to cover related business losses.

593
38:49.641 --> 38:51.434
-Will it work? -Okay, okay, okay.

594
38:51.560 --> 38:52.519
Sounds good.

595
38:52.644 --> 38:54.855
But sir, if project costs go up

596
38:54.980 --> 38:57.524
and another town snatches it, then what do we do?

597
38:57.816 --> 38:59.818
We'll be left empty-handed.

598
39:01.319 --> 39:02.654
You don't need to worry about all that.

599
39:03.446 --> 39:05.448
Now, here in Taegye-ri,

600
39:06.116 --> 39:09.369
the wind coming over the ridges is steady all year round.

601
39:09.619 --> 39:10.620
Right.

602
39:10.745 --> 39:13.623
-A location like this is really-- -[Mi-do] How do I get to the store?

603
39:17.502 --> 39:18.336
[man] Go ahead.

604
39:18.879 --> 39:20.380
Say hello to the gentleman.

605
39:20.505 --> 39:25.218
This is the wonderful lawyer from Seoul who is helping us out

606
39:25.343 --> 39:26.428
with our wind farm.

607
39:27.220 --> 39:28.471
She came out here today.

608
39:28.930 --> 39:30.515
She's on a spontaneous trip.

609
39:31.141 --> 39:33.977
What did you say you do to earn a living?

610
39:34.102 --> 39:35.562
-Unemployed. -Unemployed.

611
39:38.064 --> 39:39.024
Hello, sir.

612
39:39.482 --> 39:40.442
I'm Lee Mi-do.

613
39:47.866 --> 39:52.120
[thunder rumbling]

614
39:53.622 --> 39:55.248
[rain thrashing]

615
39:55.373 --> 39:56.333
[Tae-seung] What's going on?

616
39:57.209 --> 39:58.043
Explain.

617
39:58.627 --> 39:59.669
Didn't you check the forecast?

618
40:00.378 --> 40:01.338
No umbrella?

619
40:01.463 --> 40:02.714
Don't change the subject.

620
40:03.965 --> 40:05.508
What's going on? Tell me now.

621
40:08.220 --> 40:10.430
I saw Attorney Seo coming out of your office.

622
40:11.890 --> 40:13.099
Yes. Hello, sir.

623
40:13.225 --> 40:14.059
Yes.

624
40:14.726 --> 40:16.645
I found a lawyer for the Taegye-ri project.

625
40:17.562 --> 40:19.689
Yes. You don't need to worry at all, sir.

626
40:25.195 --> 40:26.738
[soft music playing]

627
40:28.573 --> 40:29.950
-[engine starts] -[sighs]

628
40:31.701 --> 40:32.661
Ah…

629
40:34.788 --> 40:35.872
I had no choice.

630
40:37.707 --> 40:39.125
Attorney Seo knows about us.

631
40:40.669 --> 40:42.587
It's not like I wanted to do this.

632
40:50.637 --> 40:52.013
[sighs deeply]

633
40:53.181 --> 40:58.019
I'll give you one last chance to be honest with me.

634
40:59.437 --> 41:03.233
Tae-seung, I know you so much better than you could ever imagine.

635
41:03.817 --> 41:05.568
I didn't want to know, but I do.

636
41:06.403 --> 41:07.904
So be honest with me.

637
41:12.492 --> 41:13.868
[Ju-hyeok] Can you live like this?

638
41:14.869 --> 41:18.790
Waking up and going to sleep in a place like this?

639
41:21.501 --> 41:22.627
How does it feel?

640
41:22.752 --> 41:23.962
[soft music concludes]

641
41:25.547 --> 41:28.591
The man who put me in here has no right to ask that.

642
41:29.134 --> 41:30.593
I'm considering getting you out.

643
41:33.972 --> 41:35.557
Why so sad?

644
41:38.685 --> 41:41.855
Tae-seung, you can't survive in here.

645
41:41.980 --> 41:42.856
Really.

646
41:43.523 --> 41:45.692
You could never do it.

647
41:46.526 --> 41:47.360
You know why?

648
41:49.738 --> 41:54.617
'Cause I turned you into someone who can't survive.

649
41:57.996 --> 41:58.955
Right?

650
42:00.415 --> 42:01.791
[emotional music playing]

651
42:07.797 --> 42:09.758
I can't let myself go to waste.

652
42:11.301 --> 42:13.803
I'm too good to just rot away like this, Mi-do.

653
42:14.971 --> 42:16.431
I know what it took to get here.

654
42:17.140 --> 42:19.642
I clawed like hell to crawl out of that shithole.

655
42:21.644 --> 42:22.854
If I let this go…

656
42:25.190 --> 42:26.983
I might regret it my whole life.

657
42:31.071 --> 42:32.030
I'm really sorry.

658
42:35.367 --> 42:37.285
But I don't want to be like you.

659
42:39.287 --> 42:41.915
I don't want to lose this chance to let myself go

660
42:42.040 --> 42:44.709
and feel afraid like you.

661
42:52.884 --> 42:53.802
Just leave.

662
42:56.304 --> 42:58.473
Whatever you say, it's not going to change my mind.

663
43:00.433 --> 43:01.518
Don't kid yourself.

664
43:03.561 --> 43:05.188
You think I came to persuade you?

665
43:05.647 --> 43:06.606
No.

666
43:06.940 --> 43:09.025
Seeing this will kill the feelings I have left.

667
43:09.275 --> 43:10.235
That's why I came.

668
43:11.111 --> 43:12.904
Seeing how vile you are up close,

669
43:13.196 --> 43:15.949
I'll be able to erase every feeling I have left.

670
43:16.074 --> 43:17.200
That's why I'm here.

671
43:20.578 --> 43:21.621
We have four days.

672
43:23.123 --> 43:25.708
After that, I don't want to remember a jerk like you.

673
43:27.252 --> 43:30.088
Someone far more despicable than I ever imagined.

674
43:30.713 --> 43:32.298
I don't want to remember you.

675
43:36.052 --> 43:37.011
Glad I got here.

676
43:39.305 --> 43:40.265
Good thing I came.

677
43:51.401 --> 43:52.777
[music swells]

678
43:55.280 --> 43:56.656
I want to forget you too!

679
43:58.533 --> 43:59.492
I'm the one

680
44:00.618 --> 44:02.829
who does not want to remember someone like you!

681
44:03.872 --> 44:04.831
That's great.

682
44:05.331 --> 44:07.125
Then let's both try hard to forget each other.

683
44:07.250 --> 44:09.043
-Hey! -Don't scream at me!

684
44:12.255 --> 44:14.174
Be careful with the tone you use.

685
44:14.299 --> 44:15.550
Han Tae-seung, sir.

686
44:28.855 --> 44:30.273
[emotional music concludes]

687
44:43.870 --> 44:44.746
[sighs]

688
44:44.871 --> 44:46.956
[lightning crashes]

689
44:47.081 --> 44:49.417
[thunder rumbles]

690
45:17.153 --> 45:18.363
[tender music playing]

691
45:32.418 --> 45:34.170
[line ringing]

692
45:38.841 --> 45:41.803
MR. NAMGUNG

693
45:44.806 --> 45:45.765
Hey, Namgung.

694
45:48.226 --> 45:49.185
Are you there?

695
45:55.233 --> 45:57.235
I know that you're listening.

696
46:00.572 --> 46:02.949
Are you really not coming?

697
46:05.201 --> 46:08.580
I even gave you my door code, so please come.

698
46:09.872 --> 46:15.837
The day we first met on Haemado, That's the code for the door.

699
46:18.006 --> 46:18.965
You…

700
46:20.091 --> 46:21.759
I warned you, remember?

701
46:22.594 --> 46:24.512
Don't get involved in this.

702
46:27.265 --> 46:31.060
I know you feel bad for poor Manager Eom.

703
46:32.854 --> 46:34.939
But it's already too late for him.

704
46:35.940 --> 46:37.650
It's far too late now.

705
46:39.027 --> 46:39.986
Hey!

706
46:41.362 --> 46:42.655
Are you listening?

707
46:44.157 --> 46:45.617
[Namgung] Yes, I'm listening.

708
46:49.871 --> 46:53.207
Just because you're placed on leave, you're drinking in broad daylight?

709
47:00.423 --> 47:01.883
Hey, hallucination, shut up.

710
47:02.425 --> 47:03.343
[chuckles]

711
47:03.926 --> 47:07.305
Hey, Namgung, are you listening?

712
47:10.141 --> 47:12.518
How will you face me after this?

713
47:17.899 --> 47:20.276
I always black out when I drink.

714
47:22.570 --> 47:25.448
I don't remember a single thing.

715
47:26.866 --> 47:27.992
I'm like my dad.

716
47:30.036 --> 47:35.249
That's why he was always drunk and causing trouble whenever he went.

717
47:48.054 --> 47:49.430
[tender music concludes]

718
47:49.555 --> 47:50.848
I drank seven cans.

719
47:52.642 --> 47:56.187
After five, I completely black out.

720
47:56.771 --> 47:58.106
Five is my limit.

721
48:00.566 --> 48:01.526
You sure?

722
48:03.152 --> 48:04.237
Mm-hmm.

723
48:05.738 --> 48:08.700
That's why I only drink when I'm at home.

724
48:14.497 --> 48:15.456
Why?

725
48:16.833 --> 48:17.792
Jealous?

726
48:23.423 --> 48:24.882
[sweet Korean pop song playing]

727
48:44.110 --> 48:45.111
What's this?

728
48:47.905 --> 48:49.741
Why does this feel real?

729
48:52.660 --> 48:53.995
It's so annoying.

730
49:05.339 --> 49:06.591
Just this once.

731
49:09.552 --> 49:11.471
I wanted to do this at least once.

732
49:13.890 --> 49:15.099
[Su-a groans]

733
49:15.475 --> 49:18.561
Hallucination, let go.

734
49:20.521 --> 49:21.355
Hey!

735
49:23.900 --> 49:25.318
You did nothing wrong.

736
49:28.654 --> 49:30.907
So don't ever regret it, Park Su-a.

737
49:35.745 --> 49:36.662
Great job.

738
49:39.207 --> 49:40.708
You did very, very good…

739
49:42.585 --> 49:43.628
Park Su-a.

740
49:48.925 --> 49:52.428
[chuckles softly]

741
50:31.551 --> 50:33.427
[song swells]

742
50:44.438 --> 50:47.441
CALL RECORDING: MR. NAMGUNG

743
50:48.401 --> 50:50.111
MOVE THIS RECORDING TO TRASH?

744
50:50.361 --> 50:51.654
ALL RECORDINGS

745
51:21.225 --> 51:22.727
[sweet Korean pop song concludes]

746
51:33.529 --> 51:34.989
What? I'm fine.

747
51:48.377 --> 51:49.337
Mi-do.

748
51:51.964 --> 51:53.466
Don't forget me too quickly.

749
51:55.468 --> 51:56.928
And don't forget everything.

750
51:59.847 --> 52:02.433
I'm really sorry for being this way.

751
52:06.020 --> 52:08.773
Think about me once a year.

752
52:10.983 --> 52:12.026
Or a week.

753
52:13.736 --> 52:14.987
Actually, no.

754
52:18.115 --> 52:19.867
Even three days is enough.

755
52:23.496 --> 52:24.622
Just think about me.

756
52:28.793 --> 52:32.421
Otherwise, it'll all be for naught.

757
52:35.424 --> 52:36.968
[tender music playing]

758
52:47.853 --> 52:48.813
Ah!

759
52:50.272 --> 52:51.273
Hey!

760
52:51.941 --> 52:53.275
[laughs]

761
52:54.652 --> 52:55.903
Ah! [winces]

762
52:56.028 --> 52:56.946
[groans]

763
52:59.407 --> 53:00.992
[laughs]

764
53:06.914 --> 53:07.790
[sighs]

765
53:12.712 --> 53:14.130
I'll think about you often.

766
53:17.800 --> 53:21.846
Maybe I'll think about you way more often than only sometimes.

767
53:28.352 --> 53:29.645
Just promise me one thing.

768
53:34.775 --> 53:39.488
Don't make me regret having feelings for you.

769
53:43.325 --> 53:46.328
I beg you, Tae-seung.

770
53:57.214 --> 53:58.549
[tender music concludes]

771
54:00.259 --> 54:02.636
-[groans] -[slippers shuffling]

772
54:08.934 --> 54:11.020
[door keypad beeps]

773
54:12.271 --> 54:13.439
[door lock chimes]

774
54:24.700 --> 54:25.659
We're gonna go out.

775
54:26.452 --> 54:27.411
Get ready.

776
54:30.372 --> 54:31.707
I found where Ji Su-yeon is.

777
54:34.794 --> 54:35.753
I'll go with you.

778
54:58.359 --> 54:59.568
[Su-yeon] It wasn't like that.

779
55:00.486 --> 55:02.321
I saw the files on your laptop by chance,

780
55:02.446 --> 55:04.615
and as a Hunmin Confectionery customer,

781
55:04.740 --> 55:07.284
I thought the public needed to know the information.

782
55:08.285 --> 55:11.622
You were torn about blowing the whistle, right?

783
55:12.206 --> 55:13.791
But that's wrong, isn't it?

784
55:14.208 --> 55:16.961
I know you work for them, but people have a right to know.

785
55:19.380 --> 55:23.259
Su-a, when it really matters, you only think of yourself.

786
55:24.343 --> 55:25.302
You're selfish.

787
55:26.637 --> 55:27.721
I'm selfish?

788
55:30.432 --> 55:32.685
You always say that I'm selfish.

789
55:34.186 --> 55:35.020
[scoffs softly]

790
55:35.312 --> 55:36.230
Aren't you?

791
55:36.355 --> 55:37.314
No, I'm not.

792
55:38.774 --> 55:43.362
I actually knew all along, but you meant so much to me,

793
55:44.613 --> 55:48.742
so I kept pretending not to know, just so we could stay friends.

794
55:50.619 --> 55:51.579
Why did we…

795
55:54.123 --> 55:55.082
end up like this?

796
55:57.251 --> 55:58.669
Who made me end up this way?

797
55:58.961 --> 56:00.045
You did, Su-yeon.

798
56:00.921 --> 56:02.339
You're living like this because of you.

799
56:02.464 --> 56:03.465
It's not my fault.

800
56:04.091 --> 56:05.843
Hey, Park Su-a.

801
56:05.968 --> 56:07.261
The trash you carry…

802
56:10.055 --> 56:11.307
don't dump it on me.

803
56:14.018 --> 56:14.977
It's all yours.

804
56:21.066 --> 56:22.318
The police will be calling.

805
56:23.319 --> 56:25.946
I filed charges for accessing and leaking files.

806
56:32.161 --> 56:35.080
You think you're so great, always acting so smart,

807
56:35.206 --> 56:36.207
principled, and moral?

808
56:36.999 --> 56:39.376
Do you know how suffocating it is to be near you?

809
56:40.419 --> 56:43.797
You make everyone else look bad to protect yourself.

810
56:44.715 --> 56:46.217
That's why your father left you.

811
56:47.092 --> 56:48.969
Because you disgusted him.

812
56:51.388 --> 56:52.890
[gentle music playing]

813
56:57.603 --> 56:58.479
You're done.

814
57:01.732 --> 57:02.691
You can keep going.

815
57:03.692 --> 57:04.652
I'll listen.

816
57:05.694 --> 57:07.029
[exhales deeply]

817
57:07.154 --> 57:10.032
Su-yeon, you didn't leave…

818
57:12.117 --> 57:13.410
the slightest little scratch on me.

819
57:15.162 --> 57:16.121
Because of you,

820
57:17.873 --> 57:19.333
I love myself more.

821
57:20.876 --> 57:24.546
Because of you, I'll probably be sad, hurt, and struggling for a long time.

822
57:27.299 --> 57:31.387
But even so, I won't change myself for you…

823
57:34.098 --> 57:35.349
because I wasn't wrong.

824
57:37.101 --> 57:38.310
I was right.

825
57:41.480 --> 57:43.148
I'll live better than anyone.

826
57:45.317 --> 57:46.527
I will be happy.

827
58:08.465 --> 58:09.591
I handled it well.

828
58:11.218 --> 58:12.594
I know. I saw.

829
58:15.597 --> 58:16.557
You were watching?

830
58:17.224 --> 58:18.100
Mm-hmm.

831
58:19.268 --> 58:20.352
You're so… Wait.

832
58:20.602 --> 58:22.813
Why were you watching? You're so weird.

833
58:24.565 --> 58:26.066
[Namgung] I thought you'd look cool.

834
58:27.484 --> 58:28.819
And you really were cool.

835
58:32.197 --> 58:33.157
Su-a.

836
58:37.661 --> 58:39.872
Because of you, I love myself more.

837
58:44.710 --> 58:45.669
So thank you.

838
58:49.131 --> 58:50.674
And fantasies do exist.

839
58:52.176 --> 58:53.135
Except…

840
58:54.970 --> 58:57.014
every fantasy takes a long time to unfold.

841
59:04.021 --> 59:05.064
[gentle music concludes]

842
59:08.817 --> 59:09.777
Namgung…

843
59:13.530 --> 59:14.782
is it really fine…

844
59:19.286 --> 59:20.245
if I…

845
59:22.373 --> 59:23.332
don't regret it?

846
59:28.629 --> 59:30.089
So you do remember, huh?

847
59:31.757 --> 59:36.303
I usually don't remember anything when I drink a lot.

848
59:37.221 --> 59:39.306
But maybe because you pinched me.

849
59:41.183 --> 59:42.434
I'm annoyed too.

850
59:45.771 --> 59:47.689
Then pretend you don't remember.

851
59:52.653 --> 59:54.029
I'll pretend I don't.

852
59:55.823 --> 59:57.157
Let's make eye contact.

853
59:59.660 --> 01:00:01.286
We only have three days left.

854
01:00:06.750 --> 01:00:07.709
Okay.

855
01:00:18.262 --> 01:00:19.763
[sweet music playing]

856
01:00:31.150 --> 01:00:32.234
Me too.

857
01:00:34.862 --> 01:00:39.158
Thanks to you, I love myself a little more.

858
01:00:43.370 --> 01:00:44.538
Thank you.

859
01:01:53.315 --> 01:01:54.733
[sweet music concludes]

860
01:02:09.665 --> 01:02:11.041
["Stay" playing]

861
01:02:22.970 --> 01:02:24.805
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

862
01:02:39.987 --> 01:02:41.530
Let's form an alliance.

863
01:02:41.655 --> 01:02:43.699
-How about a strategic approach? -[gasps]

864
01:02:43.824 --> 01:02:46.493
[Yeong-do] Mi-do is seeing Namgung's scumbag lawyer buddy!

865
01:02:46.618 --> 01:02:48.787
And he's dating some young side piece at work!

866
01:02:48.912 --> 01:02:50.289
Not for a single moment!

867
01:02:50.789 --> 01:02:52.457
I was never happy!

868
01:02:53.875 --> 01:02:55.627
[Su-a] You're falling for me, right?

869
01:02:55.752 --> 01:02:57.045
Then fall harder.

870
01:02:57.629 --> 01:02:58.922
[Mi-do] You did nothing wrong.

871
01:02:59.673 --> 01:03:01.091
It's all my fault.

872
01:03:04.720 --> 01:03:05.679
[song concludes]
